= Dermatology (Skin Madam - All Days)
- *Psoriasis:* Psoriasis er pictogram, koi hoy, er sathe kono arthropathy hoy naki. Plaque psoriasis findings, complications, and treatment. RA vs psoriatic arthropathy. Ei 2 ta condition e kom drug dei (MTX). Different kivabe psoriasis theke eczema o tineasis.
- *Scabies:* Scabies pictogram and treatment. Infected scabies pictogram, lesion identification, sites, features, and management. Why does itching increase at night.
- *Herpes Zoster:* Herpes Zoster pictogram. Total types of Herpes Simplex virus and VZ koy no type?. Ramsay hunt syndrome and vesicle on external auricle. Causative organism and treatment. Lesion description, does not cross midline, and complications.
- *Fungal / Tineasis:* Tineasis and herpes identification. Pictogram of tenia, primary/secondary skin lesions, and types of tenia. 10% KOH keno dei and microscope findings. Candida and systemic/topical antifungal drugs. Fungal diseases (Tinea, Pityriasis, Candidiasis), anti-fungal drugs, and Dermatophytes.
- *Urticaria / Allergy:* Acute urticaria treatment. Type 1 hypersensitivity reaction kibhabe hoy. Urticaria features, treatment, and hypersensitivity type.
- *Leprosy & Syphilis:* Skin e hypopigmentation kore emon koyekta condition. Leprosy organism, types, cardinal features, tuberculoid vs lepromatous, and nerve involvement. Z-N stain vs TB stain. Genital ulcer cause and syphilis stages. Characteristic lesions (gumma, condylomata lata), VDRL, TPHA, and Dark field microscopy.
- *Other Skin Conditions:* Chronic arsenicosis features and raindrop pattern. Acne Vulgaris pathogenesis, stages, and treatment.

= Paediatrics (Viva - All Days)
- *Malnutrition & Fluids:* Baggy pant pictogram, WHO classification, SAM criteria, and complications. Bleeding kno hoy (Vit K dependent factors). Shakir's tape, F75/F100, and refeeding safely. Cause of death in malnutrition. ROSOMAL vs ORS. Cholera saline use, severe dehydration features, and dosage calculation. IYCF components.
- *Hematology:* Thalassemia X-ray/pictogram, microcytic anemia, genetics, investigations, and treatment. Thalassemia complications, splenectomy prep, vaccines, and iron chelation. Hemophilia intrinsic pathway, X-linked, and factor VIII/IX. ITP pictogram, D/D, investigation, and treatment. IDA pictogram, severe palmar pallor, and serum ferritin/iron.
- *Respiratory & TB:* Miliary mottling X-ray. MT test and when it is negative. Gastric content collection and TB treatment. Pneumonia and bronchiolitis differences. Spacer/inhaler uses and colors (blue vs purple).
- *Cardiology:* Down syndrome pictogram, karyotype, findings, and chromosomal diseases. TOF pictogram, cyanotic vs acyanotic, squatting, and polycythemia. X-ray findings for TOF.
- *Neonatology/Neuro:* Perinatal asphyxia, resuscitation, AMBU bag parts/uses, and APGAR score. Hypoxic ischemic encephalopathy and convulsion management (phenobarbital). GBS scenario, ascending paralysis, and albumino-cytological dissociation.
- *Endo/Infectious:* Congenital Hypothyroidism pictogram, T3/T4/TSH, and mental retardation. Measles pictogram, Koplik's spot, 3 phases, SSPE, and Vit A dose. IMCI classification for measles. Kala-azar vector, PKDL, and bone marrow findings.

= Medicine Viva (Board 1 & 3 Pattern)
- *Rheumatology:* Seronegative arthritis (AS, Psoriatic), HLA-B27, and inflammatory arthritis features. Rheumatoid hand pictogram, 6 deformities, diagnostic criteria, and MTX. Monoarthritis causes, Gout vs Pseudogout, and septic arthritis. SLE, ANA positive diseases, and Sjogren's.
- *Cardiology:* ECG of Heart block causes, relation to inferior/anterior MI, pacemaker, and atropine. ECG of Anterior/Inferior MI, complications, thrombolysis, and streptokinase. ECG of Atrial Fibrillation, pulse, stroke, CHADS2-VASc, and rate limiting CCB. SVT ECG. ALVF treatment.
- *Pulmonology:* X-ray of Consolidation vs Lung abscess. Rusty vs purulent sputum, air-fluid level, and pneumonia complications. X-ray of TB, pleural effusion, and extra-pulmonary vs pulmonary. ADA, TB drugs, and hepatotoxicity (pyridoxine).
- *Neurology:* Bell's palsy pictogram, Ramsay Hunt syndrome, VZ virus, and UMNL vs LMNL. Hemiparesis, paraparesis, and cross hemiplegia. Paraplegia causes, acute transverse myelitis, and spastic vs flaccid tone.
- *Gastroenterology:* CLD stigmata, ascites causes, and hepatic encephalopathy. Acute vs Chronic pancreatitis, causes, Lipase, ERCP, and malabsorption. IBD vs IBS. Obstructive jaundice, Ca head of pancreas, and palpable gallbladder.
- *Nephrology/Endocrinology:* DM diagnosis, OGTT, and polyuria causes (DM vs DI). Hypercalcemia and Hyperkalemia treatment/ECG. Acute Renal Failure, and nephrotic vs nephritic. Multiple myeloma X-ray (punched out lesions) and hyperviscosity.

= Medicine & Paediatrics Cases (All Boards)
== Long Cases
- *CKD with DM with HTN:* Sensory component of foot examination and two-point discrimination. Romberg sign, autonomic neuropathy, and RRT.
- *CLD with Portal HTN / Variceal Bleeding:* Ascites, stigmata, and hepatitis investigations.
- *ALVF with HTN with DM / Ischemic Heart Disease:* Salient features, gallop rhythm, and basal crepitations. Orthopnea and differentiating from CCF.
- *Acute on Chronic Pancreatitis / PUD:* Pain relation to eating, weight changes, and lipase testing. Alcohol and drug causes.
- *Pneumonia with DM with HTN:* Causative agents and complications.

== Short Cases
- *Paediatrics:* Measure height/weight, plot on growth chart, and interpret percentiles. Short stature causes (familial ta shunte chay). Measure MUAC (mid point, Shakir's tape). Palpate abdomen for hepatosplenomegaly, ascites, and differentiate kidney from spleen.
- *Medicine (Neurology):* Facial nerve exam and UMNL vs LMNL. Knee/Ankle jerk and biceps jerk (root values, causes of diminished reflexes). Planter reflex and Romberg sign.
- *Medicine (Chest/Cardio):* Precordium auscultation, identify murmurs, and shifted apex beat. Basal crepitations. Respiratory percussion and auscultation (dullness, vesicular with prolonged expiration).
- *Medicine (Abdomen/General):* Spleen palpation (surgery hand positioning). Face and hand examination (clubbing, leuconychia, hepatic facies, tremor, jaundice) and assess gait. Lower limb examination for diabetic neuropathy/ulcers.